      "question_type": "mcq",
      "rationale": "Correct answer: At least 5.00 m. This is directly supported by PD 1096 2004 Revised IRR, Section 1302.",
      "explanation": "Escalator limits: ≤30° inclination, ≤38 m/min speed. Also note: escalator step width must be 560 mm–1.20 m. The 30° angle and 38 m/min speed are frequently tested together as a paired fact.",
