      "question_type": "mcq",
      "rationale": "Correct answer: 20 to 24 degrees C. This is directly supported by PD 1096 2004 Revised IRR, Section 1302.",
      "explanation": "Boiler room: 1.00 m from walls + 2 exits minimum. Both requirements apply simultaneously. Additionally, boiler rooms in non-fire-resistive buildings must have exterior walls at least 3.00 m from any adjacent structure — a third requirement for combustible-construction contexts.",
