      "question_type": "mcq",
      "rationale": "Correct answer: A Professional Electrical Engineer. This is directly supported by PD 1096 2004 Revised IRR, Section 1301.",
      "explanation": "Four permits, four professionals: PEE (electrical), RME (mechanical), RSP (sanitary), PECE (electronics). Each ancillary permit is independent — a PEE cannot sign the mechanical permit. The professional licensing laws (RA 7920 for PEE, RA 8495 for RME) define the scope of each practice.",
