      "rationale": "Correct answer: Not over 2.45 m above established grade. This is directly supported by PD 1096 2004 Revised IRR, Section 1301.",
      "explanation": "Hospital emergency power: ≤10 seconds transition. This is a hard safety threshold — surgical procedures and critical care equipment cannot tolerate longer interruptions. The 10-second standard aligns with NFPA 99 for healthcare facilities.",
